      "description": "Watch Celta Vigo vs Osasuna highlights and goals from La Liga on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 28, 2026. The La Liga clash on August 28, 2026, between Celta Vigo and Osasuna delivered a masterclass in tactical shifts and emotional volatility. Both teams entered the fray seeking to establish dominance in a fixture that would ultimately be defined by a dramatic reversal of fortunes under the bright lights of the stadium. Aspas Strikes Early for Celta Celta Vigo started the match with intent, pinning the visitors back and searching for an early breakthrough. That moment arrived in the 14th minute when the talismanic Iago Aspas showcased his enduring quality. Assisted by Miguel Roman , Aspas unleashed a clinical left-footed strike from outside the box that flew into the net, leaving the keeper stranded. The home side looked comfortable for the remainder of the first half, maintaining their 1-0 lead as they headed into the tunnel, despite several offside calls disrupting their offensive flow. The Red Card Turning Point The complexion of the game changed entirely in the 51st minute. Following a serious foul, Marcos Alonso was shown a red card after a VAR review, forcing Celta Vigo to play the final 40 minutes with ten men. Tactical adjustments followed immediately, with Aspas being sacrificed for defender Carl Starfelt . However, Osasuna wasted no time in capitalizing on their numerical advantage. In the 54th minute, Enrique Barja met a cross from Raul Garcia with a spectacular right-footed volley to level the score at 1-1. Budimir Completes the Comeback With momentum firmly on their side, Osasuna pushed for a winner. The pressure told in the 62nd minute when Javi Galan handled the ball in the penalty area, prompting the referee to point to the spot. Substitute Ante Budimir stepped up and coolly converted the penalty, sending Ionut Andrei Radu the wrong way to make it 2-1. In a frantic finish, Celta threw everything forward, earning multiple corners through Hugo Alvarez and Miguel Roman , but the Osasuna defense held firm. Budimir nearly added a third in stoppage time only to see his shot hacked off the goal line, but the job was already done as the visitors secured all three points."
